---
// The page a partner reads before asking for the trial build.
//
// It answers three questions in the order an evaluation program usually asks them: what runs
// here, what arrives, and what is owed on both sides before it travels. The build is not offered
// as a download: it is sent under an evaluation agreement, so the page states the terms and asks
// for the call. It lists no files; the evidence those carry is on the pages that describe the runs.
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';

const contact = 'mailto:demo@ktema.systems';

// The classes one build carries. The archive's own manifest states which of them it got, and a
// class that is not here is built to order rather than promised.
const platforms = [
  {
    machine: 'Part, no operating system',
    target: 'riscv32imac-unknown-none-elf',
    you: 'The header, the static library, and the worked example',
  },
  {
    machine: 'Part, no operating system',
    target: 'thumbv7em-none-eabihf',
    you: 'The header, the static library, and the worked example',
  },
  {
    machine: 'Workstation or server',
    target: 'x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu',
    you: 'Those, a shared object, a Python binding, and the daemon',
  },
  {
    machine: 'Single-board computer',
    target: 'aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu',
    you: 'Those, a shared object, a Python binding, and the daemon',
  },
];
---

<Shell
  title="Ktema trial build"
  description="The Ktema record engine as a pre-commercial evaluation build: the platforms it runs on, what arrives, and the terms it is sent under."
  crumbs={[{ label: 'Corpus Hub', href: '/' }, { label: 'Ktema trial build' }]}
>
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="hero__product"><span class="product-tag">Ktema</span></p>
    <h1>Trial build</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Ktema is the record engine: a record is found at the address its own fields compute, so a read
      maintains no index. Kletos runs verifiable execution on that base, and Krisis sets what a run may do,
      over which model, at what cost, with what authority. The upper tiers attach to the same foundation,
      and this build is the foundation, from a part with no operating system to a Linux host.
    </p>
    <p class="phase">
      <span class="phase__label">PoC partner phase</span> The build is pre-commercial and covers Ktema alone, not
      the tiers above it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Platforms</h2>
    <p class="section__lede">
      These are the classes one build carries. A port to another class, or to a board with its own storage, is built
      to order.
    </p>
    <div class="platforms-wrap">
      <table class="platforms">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Machine</th>
            <th scope="col">Target</th>
            <th scope="col">What you get</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            platforms.map((row) => (
              <tr>
                <td>{row.machine}</td>
                <td>
                  <code>{row.target}</code>
                </td>
                <td>{row.you}</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>What you receive</h2>
    <dl class="ready">
      <dt>The build</dt>
      <dd>
        A C header, a static library, and a worked example for each class above; a shared object and a Python binding
        where the class has an operating system; a daemon for each Linux class. The manifest states the classes it
        got and the ones it did not.
      </dd>
      <dt>The specification</dt>
      <dd>
        Four documents: the format, the medium, the index, and the coordinate read. They are enough to build a
        conforming implementation and to check a record you did not write.
      </dd>
      <dt>The check</dt>
      <dd>
        A digest for every file in the archive, a signature over that list, and the fingerprint of the key that made
        it.
      </dd>
    </dl>
    <p class="note">
      It runs where you put it, with no account and no network call.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Requesting it</h2>
    <p class="section__lede">
      The build that matches your machine is sent on request, under an evaluation agreement. An NDA can be signed
      before anything is shared, and the terms it is issued under travel in the archive as <code>LICENSE</code>. A
      board with its own storage reaches the engine through four storage functions and two critical-section hooks that
      the integrator supplies.
    </p>
    <p class="call">
      <a class="btn btn--accent" href={contact}>Write to us</a>
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      The archive travels with its digest, and the fingerprint is sent the same way, so what arrives can be checked
      against what was signed.
    </p>
  </section>
</Shell>

<style>
  .hero__product {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }

  /* The phase is a status, not a sentence: a label in the mono face, then what the label means. */
  .phase {
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    color: var(--fg-3);
    font-size: 0.9em;
    max-inline-size: 64ch;
  }

  .phase__label {
    margin-inline-end: 0.5em;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.85em;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .section {
    margin-block-start: 3rem;
  }

  .section h2 {
    margin-block-end: 1rem;
  }

  .section__lede {
    margin-block: 0 1.5rem;
    color: var(--fg-3);
    max-inline-size: 64ch;
  }

  /* A narrow screen scrolls the table rather than stacking it: the three columns are read
     across, and a stacked row loses the comparison the table exists for. */
  .platforms-wrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .platforms {
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 44rem;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.92em;
  }

  .platforms th,
  .platforms td {
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
    padding: 0.7rem 1.5rem 0.7rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .platforms th {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.78em;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--fg-3);
  }

  .platforms td code {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
    color: var(--fg-2);
  }

  /* What a partner is deciding about, read as a list rather than a paragraph: the three things
     that arrive are the answer, and each is one line. */
  .ready {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(10rem, max-content) 1fr;
    gap: 0.6rem 1.5rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
    max-inline-size: 74ch;
  }

  .ready dt {
    font-size: 0.95em;
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  .ready dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--fg-3);
    font-size: 0.92em;
  }

  .call {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }

  .note {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--fg-3);
    font-size: 0.88em;
    max-inline-size: 64ch;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .ready {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.15rem;
    }

    .ready dd {
      margin-block-end: 0.75rem;
    }
  }
</style>
